  "notes": "Measured on 4X-EDJ (left, 2019-04-14), fitted to the 787-9 shape; 4X-EDK (2025 right, 2024 left) shows the same scheme. The swoosh's blues blend (navy low and forward, bright blue on its upper edge): drawn as two areas. 4X-EDN (delivered 2025, one photo from below) has the lower rear body navy up to the windows, joining the fin's lower band: an airframe variant not drawn here. Aircraft names by the nose (city names, and since 2024 a Hebrew line on some) not drawn. The 787's raked wingtips carry no winglet paint.",
  "history": "New file (El Al had no scheme here). Introduced with the 787-9s from 2017; the older 737s and 777s that carried the earlier cheatline scheme have been repainted or retired, not checked here."
